2.2 Diffusion model-based inverse problem solving with gradient guidance
Suppose now that we are given a measurement y obtained through some Gaussian linear measurement process A, where our goal is to sample from the posterior distribution p(x|y). Starting from the sampling process of running the reverse SDE/ODE to sample from the prior distribution, one can modify the score function to adapt it for posterior sampling [38, 5]. By Bayes rule, ∇xt log p(xt|y) = ∇xt log p(xt) + ∇xt log p(y|xt), where ∇xt log p(xt) ≃ sθ∗ (xt). However, ∇xt log p(y|xt) is intractable. Several methods have been proposed to approximate this time-dependent likelihood, two of the most widely used being DPS [5] and ΠGDM [36]. DPS proposes the following Jensen approximation1
